sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 6, docs/reference/development-containers.md#the-default-instance): the automatic development deployment of docs/reference/deployments.md, in the default Instance's container. Every merge to the default branch reaches the default Instance, so new clones start current.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · automatic deployment tick
  %% kind: instance.deploy
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>deployment tick
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant C as Container<br/>default Instance
  Note over GW: New default-branch commit<br/>deployment tick
  %%> When:
  %%> - the default branch has a commit that the default Instance has not deployed, as today
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a deployment task with the commit, the Instance lock and a repository read token in the vault
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>development-deploy
  opt the default Instance is asleep
    SW->>N: Start the container<br/>incus start
  end
  SW->>N: Fetch the commit<br/>git fetch · read token
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - fetches on the Node and pushes the commit into the container's repository; the token never enters the container
  SW->>C: Check out the commit<br/>Ansible · tags checkout
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the same checks as a checkout default: a dirty tree refuses `deployment.checkout_dirty`, a diverged branch `deployment.branch_diverged`
  SW->>C: Run dev deploy steps<br/>Ansible · tags deploy
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the Project's development deploy steps, as `orbit`: they install changed dependencies and migrate
  %%> - restarts the Processes whose code changed
  alt every required step passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Record the seed commit
    %%> Result:
    %%> - new clones start at this commit; existing clones do not change
  else a required step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    %%> Result:
    %%> - clones keep starting at the last commit that deployed; the tick retries after a backoff, at most three times
  end
